 @MLWJ1993  My VRAM usage by web browsers often exceeds 1GB. And I don't think I have that many tabs. 

As I wrote I suspect that Windows probably does not automatically move background processes' VRAM to shared RAM, as it does with RAM/virtual memory, nor do individual applications. I wish they did, but there is nothing I can do about it.

16GB is probably more than enough, but I don't think it is exceedingly big, if you play high-end games and use other modern applications like web browsers. Probably 12GB would do for now. But I have seen games consuming 7~8GB on benchmark videos, so, having exactly 8GB means no room for other background applications.

